# UBSan source-level ignorelist (-fsanitize-ignorelist=).
#
# ONLY for confirmed-intentional bit-exact behavior the renderer relies on —
# specifically signed-integer-overflow (defined wraparound the N64 RDP emulates).
# Each entry MUST cite why it is safe. NEVER ignorelist `alignment`, OOB, or
# `function` findings: those are genuine cross-platform (arm) UB and must be
# FIXED, not suppressed.
#
# Format (clang SpecialCaseList):
#   [signed-integer-overflow]
#   fun:rdpxi_some_function   # why this wraparound is intentional + arm-safe
#   src:src/rdp/rdp/foo.cc    # (file-scoped; prefer fun: granularity)
#
# Triage outcome (2026-05-26): EMPTY by design. The survey surfaced only
# signed-integer-overflow (rasterizer/demo fixed-point accumulators) and
# left-shift-of-negative (demo fixed-point conversions). Rather than ignore
# them, the signed-overflow class is now DEFINED via -fwrapv on rdp_core +
# demo_core (host AND device), and the negative-shift sites were fixed in
# source (multiply instead of <<). So nothing needs suppressing. Kept as the
# mechanism for any genuinely-unfixable future site.
